      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Race-realists dismiss environmental criticisms by arguing that while culture and environment play a role, they are ultimately constrained by underlying genetic potential. They contend that socioeconomic disparities are themselves partially rooted in innate differences, meaning that even when controlling for environment, the biological gap persists. To distinguish between cultural and biological gaps, they posit that cultural differences are merely superficial manifestations of deeper, genetically determined cognitive capacities. Therefore, they maintain that the observed gaps are fundamentally biological, not merely circumstantial.",
